	"equipment": [
		{
			"id": "eyPnLQ37RkPU5bAL3",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark IV (Heretic)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 6: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 6 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nInterlocking plate sections reduce the usual bulky-armour penalty by 1 relative to other Marks at the GM's discretion (still requires the black carapace interface). Worn seals and joints: Weak Points 6.\n\nLore: Mark IV Maximus plate is the commonest armour of the Traitor Legions in Black Library fiction: it was the mainline suit at the end of the Heresy and nothing has replaced it for the Legions that fled into the Eye of Terror. Suits are repaired, never rebuilt, and often carry a god's mark in brass, bone or paint.\n\nDesign: DR, servo ST, weight and cost match the loyalist Mark IV (Maximus Pattern) entry, included unchanged. Weak Points 5 to 6, per the framework's Chaos armour rule (ten thousand years without a forge-temple). This is the reference traitor suit: Rubric and Plague-Fused plate below are variants of it.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Chaos",
				"Heretic Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "38000",
			"base_weight": "135 lb",
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"torso",
						"vitals",
						"groin"
					],
					"amount": 95
				},
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"arm"
					],
					"amount": 83
				},
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"leg"
					],
					"amount": 83
				},
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"neck"
					],
					"amount": 58
