		{
			"id": "eVHNGB6n09066hUp-",
			"description": "Sonic Blaster",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Noise Marines of the Emperor's Children carry sonic blasters, rifle-sized weapons that project a beam of destructive sound which shakes a target's body apart inside its armour (Codex: Chaos Space Marines, Emperor's Children and Noise Marine fiction). Their sound-obsessed users prize the shriek of a fired shot as much as its effect.\n\nDesign: Damage and rate follow the Chaos anchor: 5d(5) cr, RoF 3, range 50/150. The divisor is what lets sound shake a Marine apart inside his armour, as in the fiction; 5d(3) could never get through Mark VII plate. A first pass at 6d(5), Acc 5, Rcl 1 made Noise Marines beat loyalist Marines 38 fights in 40 in the simulator, far past the tabletop, where the sonic blaster is a bolter-class gun; 5d(5), Acc 4, Rcl 2 brings it to 26 in 40, below a Legionary's boltgun. Handling follows framework.md's Weapon handling stats. Weight 24 lb: an Astartes-scale rifle, lighter than the 38 lb Godwyn boltgun because it carries no heavy bolt and propellant. Minimum ST is the square root of 10 times 24, about 15.5, which rounds to 16, with the † for two-handed use. Acc 4: a rifle value. Rcl 2: it throws no mass, but the sound projector bucks; less than a bolter's 3. Bulk -5, an Astartes-pattern rifle. Shots 30(3) from an energy cell. Skill is Guns (Rifle), as the task requires: sound is not a beam in the framework's Skills table, and the weapon is a shoulder rifle. By exact dice, 5d(5) beats Mark VII plate (effective DR 20) on 22% of hits, its neck seal (DR 12) on 90% and carapace (DR 14) on 78%, and never Terminator plate (DR 40).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Chaos",
				"Slaanesh",
				"Noise Marine"
			],
