		{
			"id": "eYVwPdMukTD2aBnbJ",
			"description": "Combat Knife, Astartes Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Sized for a gauntleted Astartes hand; scaled to a human's shortsword rather than a human's knife. Knife edge (house rule): reduces the penalty for targeting chinks in armor (p. B400) by 2, as the stiletto does (MA228).\n\nLore: Space Marines carry a sidearm blade proportioned to their size and strength - visually a long fighting knife on a Marine's belt reads as a shortsword in a human's hand; consistently shown as a backup when a chainsword or bolt pistol isn't drawn, in Black Library Space Marine fiction from the Horus Heresy series onward.\n\nDesign: Not a bigger version of the human combat knife's stat block (that would just be the same knife with a higher min ST, understating how much blade an Astartes-scale grip actually carries) - instead it is built on the human Shortsword profile (thr+1 imp/sw+1 cut) scaled up in weight and min ST for an Astartes fist, per the framework's rule that Astartes- and human-scale versions of the same weapon type need different stats, not just a relabelling. LC1 (Astartes-issue gear) rather than the LC4 civilian knife bracket. Handling: already built on the Shortsword profile, whose Basic Set parry is 0 (a proper hilt and cross-guard, unlike the plain-bladed Munitorum knife above), so no parry change is needed here - only the plain Knife-skill weapons on this page needed the -1 correction. Weight (4 lb) and min ST (11) are unchanged, already scaled up from the human knife's 1 lb/ST 6 for an Astartes-proportioned grip. Monoedge rule (user direction): the Astartes knife's monomolecular edge takes armour divisor (3). At ST 30 a thrust or swing (5d+3) now gets through a Mark VII neck seal on 40% of hits and carapace on 22%, and still can't open a power-armoured torso.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
